id: lingering-power
name: Lingering Power
order: 1
category: mind
# A Factor Trait replaces a Secondary Racial Trait - Secondary, then, unless it names a Primary one to replace.
importance: secondary
# (1) The Past Life, asked as it is gained - a Character of this world or one named - and with it the Skill, the Attribute, the Talent
# and the base Tier of Power its effects read (racial.mjs askPastLife).
pastLife: true
description: >
  Drawing on the strength remaining deep in your soul from your past life, you have greater strength than others of your race.
text: >
  Lingering Power (Mind): Drawing on the strength remaining deep in your soul from your past life, you have greater strength than others of your race.
  (1)-[Ruling]: Upon gaining the Reincarnated Factor, you must select a Character that is deceased (with the permission of your ARC) to be your ‘Past Life’. Your ‘Past Life’ no longer exists as an independent Character.
  (2)-[Passive]: Gain a Skill Rank in the Skill with the highest number of Skill Ranks among your Past Life’s Skills (if it’s a tie, you decide).
  (3)-[Passive]: Increase the Attribute Score of the Attribute that your Past Life had the highest Attribute Score in by 2 (if it’s a tie, you decide).
  (4)-[Passive]: Gain a Talent that your Past Life possessed and you meet the Prerequisites for.
  (5)-[Triggered/Power, 1/Encounter]: Increase your Combat Rolls by 2(bT), using your Past Life’s base Tier of Power to calculate the bonus, until the end of your next turn.

---

# (1) The ARC's permission, and the Past Life no longer played, are the table's. (4) The Talent chosen with it, given as it is gained
# and kept as a Racial Trait's Talent is; its Prerequisites the table's.
[passive]
# (2), (3) As they were answered.
skill.$pastSkill.ranks += 1;
$pastAttribute.score += 2;

# (5) 2(bT) by the Past Life's base Tier, till the end of your next turn (chat.mjs lingeringPower). Automatic by default, its
# Triggered/Automatic button.
[triggered/power, 1/encounter, effect 5]
lingeringPower();
